### 7.3 Upgrade Mechanism

#### How Upgrades Work

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    UPGRADE MECHANISM                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Before Upgrade:
    TokenProxy
        │
        ├─ getImplementationAuthority() → 0xIA
        │
    0xIA (Implementation Authority)
        │
        └─ getTokenImplementation() → 0xTokenV1
        
    User Call: proxy.transfer(...)
        ↓
    Delegatecall to 0xTokenV1
        ↓
    TokenV1 logic executes with proxy's storage


After Upgrade (set new implementation):
    Owner calls: IA.setTokenImplementation(0xTokenV2)
    
    TokenProxy (unchanged!)
        │
        ├─ getImplementationAuthority() → 0xIA (same)
        │
    0xIA (Implementation Authority)
        │
        └─ getTokenImplementation() → 0xTokenV2 ⬅ UPDATED
        
    User Call: proxy.transfer(...)
        ↓
    Delegatecall to 0xTokenV2 ⬅ NEW LOGIC
        ↓
    TokenV2 logic executes with proxy's storage (preserved)
```

#### Upgrade Process

**Step 1: Deploy New Implementation**
```solidity
TokenV2 newImpl = new TokenV2();
```

**Step 2: Update Implementation Authority**
```solidity
implementationAuthority.setTokenImplementation(address(newImpl));
```

**Step 3: All Proxies Automatically Use New Logic**
- No need to update individual proxies
- Storage preserved
- Existing token holders unaffected

#### Upgrade Safety

**Storage Collisions Prevention**:
```solidity
contract TokenStorage {
    // Existing storage
    mapping(address => uint256) internal _balances;
    // ...
    
    // Gap for future variables
    uint256[49] private __gap;
}
```

**New Version Can Add**:
```solidity
contract TokenV2Storage is TokenStorage {
    // New storage (uses __gap space)
    mapping(address => uint256) internal _newFeature;
    
    // Reduced gap
    uint256[48] private __gap;
}
```

**⚠️ NEVER DO**:
```solidity
// ❌ BAD: Changes existing storage layout
contract TokenV2StorageBad is TokenStorage {
    mapping(address => uint256) internal _newFeature;  // Inserted BEFORE existing
    mapping(address => uint256) internal _balances;    // SHIFTED position!
}
```

