## 9. Storage Contracts

### Storage Pattern

T-REX uses dedicated storage contracts to separate state from logic:

**TokenStorage.sol**:
```solidity
contract TokenStorage {
    mapping(address => uint256) internal _balances;
    mapping(address => mapping(address => uint256)) internal _allowances;
    uint256 internal _totalSupply;
    
    string internal _tokenName;
    string internal _tokenSymbol;
    uint8 internal _tokenDecimals;
    address internal _tokenOnchainID;
    
    mapping(address => bool) internal _frozen;
    mapping(address => uint256) internal _frozenTokens;
    bool internal _tokenPaused;
    
    IIdentityRegistry internal _tokenIdentityRegistry;
    IModularCompliance internal _tokenCompliance;
    
    uint256[49] private __gap;
}
```

**IRStorage.sol**, **TIRStorage.sol**, **CTRStorage.sol**, **MCStorage.sol** - Similar pattern

**Benefits**:
-  Clear separation of concerns
-  Easier to understand state variables
-  Safer upgrades (explicit storage layout)
-  Reusable across implementation versions

