## 12. Contract Interaction Flows

### Flow 1: Token Transfer

```
User calls: token.transfer(to, 100)
    ↓
Token._transfer()
    ├─ Check: !paused ✓
    ├─ Check: !frozen[from] ✓
    ├─ Check: !frozen[to] ✓
    ├─ Check: sufficient unfrozen balance ✓
    │
    ├─ IdentityRegistry.isVerified(to)
    │   ├─ IdentityRegistryStorage.storedIdentity(to)
    │   ├─ ClaimTopicsRegistry.getClaimTopics()
    │   ├─ TrustedIssuersRegistry.getTrustedIssuers()
    │   └─ OnchainID.getClaim() + verify signature
    │   └─ Return true 
    │
    ├─ ModularCompliance.canTransfer(from, to, 100)
    │   ├─ Module1.moduleCheck() → true
    │   ├─ Module2.moduleCheck() → true
    │   └─ Module3.moduleCheck() → true
    │   └─ Return true 
    │
    ├─ Update: _balances[from] -= 100
    ├─ Update: _balances[to] += 100
    ├─ Emit: Transfer(from, to, 100)
    │
    └─ ModularCompliance.transferred(from, to, 100)
        ├─ Module1.moduleTransferAction()
        ├─ Module2.moduleTransferAction()
        └─ Module3.moduleTransferAction()
```

### Flow 2: Investor Onboarding

```
1. Investor creates OnchainID
    IdFactory.createIdentity(investorWallet, "salt")
    
2. KYC Provider issues claim
    KYCProvider.addClaim(investorOnchainID, topic=1, data, signature)
    
3. Agent registers identity
    IdentityRegistry.registerIdentity(wallet, onchainID, country)
    └─ IdentityRegistryStorage.addIdentityToStorage()
    
4. Agent mints tokens
    Token.mint(wallet, 1000)
    ├─ Check: isVerified(wallet) ✓
    ├─ Update: _balances[wallet] += 1000
    └─ ModularCompliance.created(wallet, 1000)
        └─ Modules update supply tracking
```

### Flow 3: Compliance Module Update

```
1. Owner adds module
    ModularCompliance.addModule(newModule)
    ├─ Check: module.canComplianceBind(compliance)
    ├─ Call: module.bindCompliance(compliance)
    └─ Add to _modules[]
    
2. Owner configures module
    ModularCompliance.callModuleFunction(
        abi.encodeWithSignature("setLimit(uint256)", 1000000),
        newModule
    )
    
3. Future transfers now check this module
    Transfer → canTransfer() → newModule.moduleCheck()
```

### Flow 4: Implementation Upgrade

```
1. Deploy new implementation
    TokenV2 newImpl = new TokenV2();
    
2. Update implementation authority
    ImplementationAuthority.setTokenImplementation(address(newImpl))
    
3. All token proxies now use V2
    TokenProxy
        ├─ getImplementationAuthority() → IA
        └─ IA.getTokenImplementation() → newImpl 
        
4. Next user call uses new logic
    User: proxy.transfer()
        ↓ delegatecall
    TokenV2 logic executes
```

